SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade Oct
 ober Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Attention Trading Partners: MIHMS Upgrade October Payme
 nt Cycle Changes and System Access Limitations\nAttention Trading Partners
 : MIHMS Upgrade October Payment Cycle Changes and System Access Limitation
 s\nAug 21\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, the Office of MaineCare 
 Services (OMS) is preparing to launch an upgraded version of MIHMS\, Maine
 Care’s claims processing system. The upgrade is currently scheduled to g
 o live on October 10\, 2026. To support a smooth transition\, OMS must imp
 lement temporary system access limitations and adjustments to payment cycl
 es in October.\nFrom Friday\, October 2 at 8:00 PM until Monday\, October 
 12 at 8:00 AM\, MIHMS will be in a “data freeze” while OMS completes f
 inal system readiness and transition activities.\nChanges to October payme
 nt cycles:\nReview this information and plan billing accordingly to prepar
 e for the transition.\nPayment Cycle Date\nPayment Impact\nClaim Submissio
 n Deadline for Inclusion in Payment Cycle*\nWednesday\, 9/30/26\nLast regu
 lar payment before the data freeze\nFriday\, 9/25/26\, 5:00 AM\nThursday\,
  10/1/26\nExtra\npayment before the data freeze\nWednesday\, 9/30/26\, 5:0
 0 AM\nThere will be no payment on Wednesday\, October 7.\nThursday\, 10/15
 /26\nFirst payment after data freeze\, in upgraded system\nSecure File Tra
 nsfer Protocol (SFTP) submission: Continuous through data freeze up to Tue
 sday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nPortal submission:\nBefore data freeze: Friday\
 , 10/2/26\, 7:59 PM\nAfter data freeze: Tuesday\, 10/13/26\, 2:00 PM\nWedn
 esday\, 10/21/26\nRegular payment\, in upgraded system\nFriday\, 10/16/26\
 , 5:00 AM\n*As always\, timely submission does not guarantee that the clai
 m will process in time for the next payment cycle. OMS may take up to 30 d
 ays to process and pay a claim\, depending on any edits or issues that may
  cause the claim to pend for manual review\, as well as other processing r
 equirements that may requi\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provi
 der-bulletins/attention-trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-cyc
 le-changes-and-system-access
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/attention-
 trading-partners-mihms-upgrade-october-payment-cycle-changes-and-system-ac
 cess
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
