SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Maine Blood Donation Day - September 4
DESCRIPTION:WHEREAS\n\, the State of Maine is committed to ensuring the sa
 fety and security of all those living in and visiting our state\; and\nWHE
 REAS\n\, a sufficient blood supply is a public health issue both locally a
 nd nationally\, and our hospitals and medical centers need a readily avail
 able supply for our residents and visitors\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, one blood do
 nation can help save more than one life\, and although most of the U.S. po
 pulation is eligible to donate blood\, only about 3 percent actually do\; 
 and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine is home to many organizations committed to raising 
 awareness about the importance of blood donation\, including the American 
 Red Cross\; and\nWHEREAS\n\, Maine Blood Donation Day effectively serves t
 o remind us that we need to constantly replenish our blood supply through 
 donation and community awareness\;\nNOW THEREFORE\n\, be it resolved that 
 I\, Janet T. Mills\, Governor of the State of Maine\, do hereby proclaim S
 eptember 4th\, 2026 as\nMaine Blood Donation Day\nthroughout the State of 
 Maine\, and I urge all Maine people to support our local blood drives as s
 aving lives and protecting our residents is our primary goal.\nIn testimon
 y whereof\, I have caused\nthe Great Seal of the State to be\nhereunto aff
 ixed GIVEN under my\nhand at Augusta this seventeenth day\nof August Two T
 housand Twenty-Six\nhttp://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents
 /proclamations/2026-08-maine-blood-donation-day-september-4
URL:http://www.maine.gov/governor/mills/official_documents/proclamations/2
 026-08-maine-blood-donation-day-september-4
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
