UID:a6d5de8d8880d1c3@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260814T024310Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Pharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denia
 ls: Enroll to Avoid Denials
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Pharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denials: Enroll
  to Avoid Denials\nPharmacy Prior Authorization and Claims Denials: Enroll
  to Avoid Denials\nAug 13\, 2026\nAs\npreviously communicated\n\, billing 
 providers must include the National Provider Identifier (NPI) of an enroll
 ed MaineCare practitioner who is ordering\, prescribing\, or referring on 
 claims submitted to MaineCare. This is a federal requirement. In the next 
 few months\, MaineCare will begin to\ndeny pharmacy PAs\nfor prescriptions
  written by providers who are not enrolled with MaineCare\, and will subse
 quently begin to\ndeny Point of Sale pharmacy claims\nthat do not have the
  NPI of an enrolled prescriber on the claim.\nThis requirement is for:\nAl
 l prescription claims\, including Point of Sale claims\nClinical laborator
 ies for ordered tests\nImaging centers for ordered imaging procedures\nDur
 able Medical Equipment\, Prosthetics\, Orthotics and Supplies (DMEPOS)\nEn
 roll with MaineCare today!\nMake sure your patients can continue to get th
 eir medications covered by ensuring any unenrolled prescribing providers c
 omplete an online application through the\nHealth PAS Online Portal\n. Pr
 oviders that do not plan to seek MaineCare reimbursement may continue pres
 cribing medications to MaineCare members by enrolling specifically as a No
 n-Billing\, Ordering\, Prescribing or Referring (NOPR) provider\, which is
  a shorter process. The NOPR enrollment is faster and requires less docume
 ntation than a regular MaineCare enrollment – and is free to complete.\n
 We encourage unenrolled prescribers to start by visiting the\nProvider Enr
 ollment & Revalidation webpage\nfor helpful resources to guide you through
  the enrollment process.\nContact us for assistance.\nFor assistance with 
 the enrollment process\, please contact Provider Services by\nemail\nor ca
 ll 1-866-690-5585\, Option 2. TTY users dial 711.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/d
 hhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/pharmacy-prior-authorization-and-clai
 ms-denials-enroll-avoid-denials-2026-08-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/pharmacy-p
 rior-authorization-and-claims-denials-enroll-avoid-denials-2026-08-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:442bb4ea8a94177a@role-healthcare-human-services.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260813T191732Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Registration is Open for the 2026 MaineCare P
 rovider Conference
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Registration is Open for the 2026 MaineCare Provider Co
 nference\nRegistration is Open for the 2026 MaineCare Provider Conference\
 nAug 13\, 2026\nJoin colleagues from across Maine for the inaugural\n2026 
 MaineCare Provider Conference\n—a dynamic day of learning\, collaboratio
 n\, and connection. Centered on the theme\n"Stronger Together: Navigating 
 Change Through Collaboration\,"\nthis conference brings together providers
  from across the MaineCare community to share innovative practices\, explo
 re emerging challenges\, and strengthen partnerships that improve care for
  the people we serve.\nThis conference is made possible through support fr
 om Maine's Rural Health Transformation Program (RHTP)\, a federal initiati
 ve that helps strengthen rural healthcare by improving access to care\, su
 pporting the healthcare workforce\, modernizing healthcare systems\, and a
 dvancing innovative models of care across the state. The conference reflec
 ts these goals by creating opportunities for providers to learn from one a
 nother\, build stronger partnerships\, and share strategies that improve c
 are for MaineCare members.\nDesigned for professionals across primary care
 \, behavioral health\, oral health\, community support services\, and othe
 r disciplines\, the conference features interactive presentations\, practi
 cal strategies\, and real-world solutions that participants can immediatel
 y apply in their work. Whether you're looking to expand your knowledge\, e
 xchange ideas with peers\, or build new connections across Maine's healthc
 are and social service systems\, this conference offers valuable opportuni
 ties to learn from one another and shape the future of care.\nThe conferen
 ce welcomes participants in all roles with MaineCare provider organization
 s\n\, including:\nClinicians\nAdministrators\nCare coordinators\nProgram s
 taff\nQuality improvement\nprofessionals\nOther team members who support M
 aine\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/registra
 tion-open-2026-mainecare-provider-conference-2026-08-13
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/registrati
 on-open-2026-mainecare-provider-conference-2026-08-13
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
